==English==

{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|antibiotique|lang=fr}}, coined in 1889 by P. [[w:Vuillemin|Vuillemin]] from {{term|anti-|lang=fr}} and {{term|biotique|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|βιωτικός|tr=biōtikós||concerning or relating to life|lang=grc}} (from {{term|βίος||life|tr=bíos|lang=grc}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*gʷeih₃w-||to live}}), perhaps influenced by {{term|ἀντίϐιος||opposed|tr=antíbios|lang=grc}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˌæn.ti.baɪˈɒt.ɪk/|/ˌæn.taɪ.baɪˈɒt.ɪk/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˌæn.taɪ.baɪˈɑ.tɪk/|/ˌæn.tə.baɪˈɑ.tɪk/}}
* {{rhymes|ɒtɪk}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|pharmacology|lang=en}} Any [[substance]] that can [[destroy]] or [[inhibit]] the [[growth]] of [[bacteria]] and similar [[microorganism]]s.

====Hyponyms====
* See also [[Wikisaurus:antibiotic]]

